      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve $7^{x+7} = 8^x$, first raise both sides of the equation to the power of $x$:\n$7^{x^2+7x} = 8^x$.\nNow, take the $x$th root of both sides of the equation:\n$7^{x+7} = \\sqrt[x]8$.\nSince the bases on both sides of the equation are equal, the exponents must be equal as well. Therefore,\n$x + 7 = \\frac{\\log_b 8}x$.\nNow, isolate $x$ in the equation:\n$x^2 + 7x - \\frac{\\log_8 b}{x} = 0$.\nWith this equation solved, we can see that $\\boxed{b}}=\\boxed{\\frac{8}{7}}$.",
